cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference or use the OpenCoast software, you can use this citation.
  This citation describes the software, not the legal validity or licensing
  of any hosted coastal access record.
type: software
title: "OpenCoast: Open-source coastal access map"
abstract: >-
  OpenCoast is an open-source web application for community-reviewed coastal
  access information. Contributors can anonymously propose beach and coastal
  areas, routes to shore, and access points with descriptions, conditions,
  and supporting sources. Moderators review proposals before publication.
  Records distinguish access status from evidence strength and retain review
  dates and revision history. The map supports global submissions; reviewed
  coverage depends on community contributions. The software is MIT licensed;
  hosted access records and private evidence have separate rights.
authors:
  - family-names: Jussmann
    given-names: Kristofer
    website: "https://github.com/Ker102"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ker102/opencoast"
url: "https://opencoast-web.vercel.app/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - coastal access
  - public beach access
  - coastal access rights
  - routes to shore
  - community mapping
  - civic technology
  - geospatial
  - OpenStreetMap
  - MapLibre
  - PostGIS
